 "title": "PPO under NEAT's rules",
 "why": "Until now PPO was not judged like NEAT. It trained on 1000-frame episodes (laps over 20 s never finished),\nkept whichever checkpoint scored best on 3 random tracks, used 4 of the 8 CPU threads, and drove without\nNEAT's action smoothing. Here it follows the shared rulebook: 2000-frame episodes, training tracks from the\nsame pool, the same lap check on the 5 validation tracks to choose the kept model, the same 0.1 smoothing,\nand 8 parallel envs. Run with two seeds so luck shows. Otherwise p06's recipe.",
